silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenscolimitapex silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensColimitApex is the concrete household cat Mittens, treated as the colimit apex of the household-side diagram D_Mittens whose typed legs the transport functor F must preserve. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#functorialtransportnamed silm:hasLongDescription "The FunctorialTransportNamed is the named transport functor F from the household category C to the schema category D, sending each ontology arrow to a typed schema arrow. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#transportedmittensapex silm:hasLongDescription "The TransportedMittensApex is the schema-side image of Mittens under F, the cocone apex through which every transported household-side leg must factor. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F(Mittens)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenssourcediagram a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittenssourcediagram" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenssourcediagram silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensSourceDiagram is the household-side diagram on Mittens whose objects are the typed household-side legs (type, taxonPath, quality, evidence, process, role, measurement). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#preservationcomparisonmap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#preservationcomparisonmap" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#preservationcomparisonmap silm:hasLongDescription "The PreservationComparisonMap is the comparison map colim(F o D_Mittens) -> F(colim D_Mittens) whose isomorphism is the preservation audit point. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'chi_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensbodymassquality a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittensbodymassquality" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensbodymassquality silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensBodyMassQuality is the body-mass quality leg of Mittens recorded by the household; F must preserve this typed leg into the schema category. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'BodyMassQuality', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensevidencerecord a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittensevidencerecord" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensevidencerecord silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensEvidenceRecord is the household-side evidence record about Mittens that the transport must keep linked to F(Mittens). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'HouseVetRecord', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensmicrochipid a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittensmicrochipid" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensmicrochipid silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensMicrochipId is Mittens' microchip identifier (9-digit string) used by the household for unique row identification across vet records. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'MicrochipId', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenspetrole a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittenspetrole" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittenspetrole silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensPetRole is the household role arrow naming Mittens as the household pet; the schema image must keep this typed role. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'HouseholdRole', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensmeasurementrecord a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.flat.sections.01_thesis.concrete_anchor#mittensmeasurementrecord" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_flat_sections_01_thesis_concrete_anchor#mittensmeasurementrecord silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensMeasurementRecord is the measurement-record arrow that binds Mittens to a body-mass measurement; transport must keep the arrow direction intact. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'MeasurementRecord', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
